n Wine Group) to join her for a conversation about a number of topics in wine industry finance including: the sale of his firm to a national company earlier this year, new rules in accounting that may affect wineries, how he helps his clients with banking relationships, and more. Carol shares her observations about the current state of the wine M&#38;A market.", "published_at": "2026-10-13 23:51:07+00:00", "source_name": "Wine Industry Advisor", "source_type": "media", "language": "en", "content_type": "market_report", "country": "US", "continent": "NEW_WORLD", "region": "Americas/North/USA", "producer_role": "trade_media", "trust_tier": "T3_professional", "info_purpose": ["P2_market_analysis"], "collection_tier": "C1_rss"}
{"id": "https://wineindustryadvisor.com/?p=170930", "url": "https://wineindustryadvisor.com/2026/10/13/pedro-parra-we-need-to-replant-burgundy-the-system-isnt-working/", "title": "Pedro Parra: We need to replant Burgundy, the system isn’t working", "summary": "<img alt=\"\" class=\"webfeedsFeaturedVisual wp-post-image\" height=\"406\" src=\"https://win-advisor-media-library.s3.us-west-1.amazonaws.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/13085007/3cafa039f9ed14f66104692a072d48a0c0e9eaa0-1400x1050-1-640x406.jpg\" style=\"display: block; margin: auto; margin-bottom: 1px;\" title=\"the-buyer.net\" width=\"640\" /><p><img alt=\"\" class=\"attachment-post-thumbnail size-post-thumbnail wp-post-image\" height=\"759\" src=\"https://win-advisor-media-library.s3.us-west-1.amazonaws.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/13085007/3cafa039f9ed14f66104692a072d48a0c0e9eaa0-1400x1050-1.jpg\" title=\"the-buyer.net\" width=\"1195\" /></p>A rare London appearance by leading terroir consultant turned winemaker, Pedro Parra, for a seminar and tasting tied to the publication of the second edition of his book Terroir Footprints turned into a troubling look at the future of winemaking in the face of climate change. For a start, the wine world’s most prominent terroiriste thinks traditional viticultural techniques are becoming obsolete as climate change is causing rising alcohol levels in wine and the loss of regional typicity, permanently affecting historic regions such as Burgundy and Montalcino. Peter Dean reports.", "content": "<img alt=\"\" class=\"webfeedsFeaturedVisual wp-post-image\" height=\"406\" src=\"https://win-advisor-media-library.s3.us-west-1.amazonaws.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/13085007/3cafa039f9ed14f66104692a072d48a0c0e9eaa0-1400x1050-1-640x406.jpg\" style=\"display: block; margin: auto; margin-bottom: 1px;\" title=\"the-buyer.net\" width=\"640\" /><p><img alt=\"\" class=\"attachment-post-thumbnail size-post-thumbnail wp-post-image\" height=\"759\" src=\"https://win-advisor-media-libra